  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It would help that for the case of VRChat to have software decoding be masked onto different CPU cores than on the main threads to have as minimal of a performance impact as possible. Having this separated from the main launch option for CPU affinity would ensure that those that have purchased the newest Ryzen 9 X3D chips will be able to get maximize their frame rate from the V-Cache chiplet while letting the second chiplet take care of the video decoding if there are video players in the world.",
